# Next steps - using scvi-tools with GPU 
Made a test script (courtesy of chatgpt)
$ cd  /project/musclehca/ccohen/gpu-test
$ nano scvi-tools-test.py
Start an interactive node
$ srun --partition=gpu --gpus 1 --cpus-per-task 5 --mem 16G -t 01:00:00 --pty bash -l
Load the conda env
$ mamba activate scvi-tools
Run the task interactively
$ python scvi-tools-test.py

To run as a job
Create job script
$ nano jobscript.sh
NB this loads conda and then activates the conda env in the job script. 
Then it runs the job. 

Need to bear this in mind for future pipelines. 


